From: mi8 <mi8@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mi8-0178: clear CS_REQUIRE_LV for the window server

dyld refuses to load the EAGL bridge into backboardd: the daemon is exec'd
seventeen times with no crash report, which is dyld exiting because library
validation rejects a library that is not signed by Apple. The flag is cleared
for that one binary, next to the CS_DEBUGGED setting of 0177.

---
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -5790,6 +5790,14 @@
 		 * nothing clears this bit on the way.
 		 */
 		imgp->ip_csflags |= CS_DEBUGGED;
+		/*
+		 * A platform binary carries CS_REQUIRE_LV, and library validation then
+		 * admits only libraries signed by Apple: the bridge in /topaz/lib is
+		 * ad-hoc signed, so dyld refuses it and the window server exits during
+		 * startup (seventeen execs, not one crash). Clear it for this one binary.
+		 */
+		imgp->ip_csflags &= ~CS_REQUIRE_LV;
+		printf("sweet: backboardd may load a library that is not Apple's\n");
 		printf("sweet: backboardd is marked debuggable so dyld takes its DYLD_* variables\n");
 		static const char *const extra[] = {
 			SWEET_GLLOAD_MX_ENV, SWEET_DYLD_PRINT_ENV, SWEET_DYLD_TOFILE_ENV
